  4233	    /// It is deliberately *not* claimed to gate a mutation that applies at every width — the two
  4234	    /// arms would move together, since a scalar instance is `W = 1` and therefore uniform too.
  4235	    /// Those are gated by the frozen E12 pins (which a moved scalar digest breaks immediately) and
  4236	    /// by `a_mixed_lookahead_cohort_falls_back_bit_identically`, whose bank lanes run the per-lane
  4237	    /// body against scalar twins running this one.
  4238	    ///
  4239	    /// The E12 corpus already carries this path at the digest level — cases 2 and 3 give every lane
  4240	    /// the same lookahead, so they take it at W4 and W8 while cases 0, 1 and 4 take the fallback —
  4241	    /// but a pinned digest says *which* bits, not *why*, and this test names the why.
  4242	    #[test]
  4243	    fn a_uniform_cohort_renders_exactly_the_per_lane_path() {
  4244	        let tracks: Vec<[InitialParameterValue; PARAMETER_COUNT * 2]> = (0..8)
  4245	            .map(|lane| values_with(-6.0 - lane as f32, 100.0, 5.0))
  4246	            .collect();
  4247	        cohort_run(&tracks, 6, None).assert_lane_identity("uniform cohort");
  4248	    }
  4249	
  4250	    /// **A cohort with one differently prepared lookahead falls back, bit for bit.**
  4251	    ///
  4252	    /// Issue #182 S1, the shape leg of [`lanes_uniform`]. Seven lanes at 5 ms and one at 1 ms is
  4253	    /// the adversarial shape rather than eight distinct ones: a gate that compared only the first
  4254	    /// two lanes, or only `window` and not `box_offset`, would still reject eight distinct
  4255	    /// lookaheads and would wrongly accept this.
  4256	    ///
  4257	    /// Red mutation: drop the shape leg, `state.lane.iter().all(..)`, from `lanes_uniform`. The
  4258	    /// odd lane is then rendered with lane 0's 241-sample window instead of its own 49-sample one,
  4259	    /// and diverges from its scalar twin inside the first block. (The phase leg does not cover
  4260	    /// this: every lane starts a fresh cohort at phase 0, so the first block is admitted before
  4261	    /// the differing windows have had a chance to desync the phases.)
  4262	    ///
  4263	    /// It is also the crate's **cross-path** gate, which is worth stating because it is not
  4264	    /// obvious from the name. The bank arm falls back to the per-lane body for all eight lanes,
  4265	    /// while every scalar twin is `W = 1` and therefore runs `sliding_minimum_uniform`. So the
  4266	    /// seven lanes that are not the odd one out compare the uniform body against the per-lane body
  4267	    /// on the same samples, and mutations *inside* the uniform body are red here: `suffix.min(..)`
  4268	    /// → `suffix.max(..)`, `for _ in 0..window` → `0..window - 1`, `state.phase.fill(position + 1)`
  4269	    /// → `fill(position)`, and `state.lane[0].box_offset` → `end_offset` in the uniform gather.
  4270	    #[test]
  4271	    fn a_mixed_lookahead_cohort_falls_back_bit_identically() {
  4272	        let mut tracks: Vec<[InitialParameterValue; PARAMETER_COUNT * 2]> =
  4273	            (0..8).map(|_| values_with(-6.0, 100.0, 5.0)).collect();
  4274	        tracks[3] = values_with(-6.0, 100.0, 1.0);
  4275	        cohort_run(&tracks, 6, None).assert_lane_identity("mixed lookahead cohort");
  4276	    }
  4277	
  4278	    /// **The two channels of a uniform cohort keep their own van Herk phases.**
  4279	    ///
  4280	    /// Closes the adversarial verifier's M-A finding. Round 2 R1(a) moved `prefix` and `phase` out
  4281	    /// of the arena and into block locals, written back once at the end of
  4282	    /// [`limiter_block_uniform`]. The `round2-1` and `round2-2` mutation rows gate a **dropped**
  4283	    /// write-back; nothing gated a **crossed** one. Writing `right`'s phase into `left` at the
  4284	    /// block end survives every other test in this crate while moving rendered bits, and this is
  4285	    /// the test that does not.
  4286	    ///
  4287	    /// Red mutation (M-A): `left.phase.fill(left_phase)` → `left.phase.fill(right_phase)` at the
  4288	    /// block-end write-back of `limiter_block_uniform`.
  4289	    ///
  4290	    /// # Why the obvious gates cannot reach it
  4291	    ///
  4292	    /// The crossing is only observable when the two channels are at *different* window positions,
  4293	    /// which needs a per-channel lookahead split — every other test in the crate prepares both
  4294	    /// channels alike, and there the crossed value is the value being overwritten. And once the
  4295	    /// split exists, neither of the crate's two standing comparison shapes helps:
  4296	    ///
  4297	    /// * **Cross-width** (`lane_identity_holds_across_widths`, `assert_lane_identity`) compares a
  4298	    ///   bank against scalar twins, and a scalar instance is `W = 1` and therefore uniform by
  4299	    ///   construction — it runs the same crossed write-back. Both widths corrupt identically and
  4300	    ///   agree.
  4301	    /// * **Partition invariance** compares one long block against several short ones. `right`'s
  4302	    ///   phase is uncorrupted and advances one step per frame, so at any shared block boundary it
  4303	    ///   is `frames mod Wb_right` whatever the partition was; the corrupted `left` inherits it and
  4304	    ///   re-syncs. Both partitions corrupt identically and agree.
  4305	    ///
  4306	    /// So the oracle has to be a rendering of the same asymmetric configuration that does **not**
  4307	    /// run the uniform write-back. The per-lane fallback body is exactly that: it writes each
  4308	    /// lane's phase from that lane's own `sliding_minimum`, per channel, and shares no code with
  4309	    /// the crossed line. Both arms below are W8 banks over the same signal; lane 7 of the oracle
  4310	    /// arm carries a third, different *left* lookahead, which makes `lanes_uniform(left)` false
  4311	    /// and sends the whole bank down the fallback. Lanes 0 through 6 are prepared identically in
  4312	    /// the two arms, so their rendered samples must agree to the bit.
  4313	    #[test]
  4314	    fn the_two_channels_of_a_uniform_cohort_keep_their_own_phases() {
  4315	        const BLOCKS: usize = 16;
  4316	        const LANES: usize = 8;
  4317	        // The three windows this test needs to be distinct. Asserted rather than assumed: if the
  4318	        // clamp in `LaneShape::new` ever swallowed one of them, the comparison below would still
  4319	        // pass and would be gating nothing.
  4320	        let shape = Shape::new(48_000).expect("shape");
  4321	        let window = |milliseconds: f32| {
  4322	            LaneShape::new(lookahead_samples(milliseconds, 48_000, shape.n), &shape).window
  4323	        };
  4324	        assert_ne!(
  4325	            window(5.0),
  4326	            window(1.0),
  4327	            "the two channels must sit at different window lengths for a crossed phase to show"
  4328	        );
  4329	        assert_ne!(
  4330	            window(3.0),
  4331	            window(5.0),
  4332	            "the odd lane must differ from the cohort or the oracle arm stays uniform"
  4333	        );
  4334	
  4335	        // Subject: every lane the same asymmetric program, so both channels are internally uniform
  4336	        // and the bank takes `limiter_block_uniform`.
  4337	        let subject: Vec<[InitialParameterValue; PARAMETER_COUNT * 2]> = (0..LANES)
  4338	            .map(|_| values_split(-6.0, 100.0, 5.0, 1.0))
  4339	            .collect();
  4340	        // Oracle: lane 7's *left* lookahead differs, so `lanes_uniform(left)` is false and both
  4341	        // channels take the per-lane body. Lanes 0..7 are byte-identical to the subject's.
  4342	        let mut oracle = subject.clone();
  4343	        oracle[7] = values_split(-6.0, 100.0, 3.0, 1.0);
  4344	
  4345	        let (subject_left, subject_right) = bank_planes(&subject, BLOCKS);
  4346	        let (oracle_left, oracle_right) = bank_planes(&oracle, BLOCKS);
  4347	
  4348	        for lane in 0..LANES - 1 {
  4349	            for frame in 0..BLOCKS * 128 {
  4350	                let index = frame * LANES + lane;
  4351	                assert_eq!(
  4352	                    subject_left[index].to_bits(),
  4353	                    oracle_left[index].to_bits(),
  4354	                    "left lane {lane} frame {frame}"
  4355	                );
  4356	                assert_eq!(
  4357	                    subject_right[index].to_bits(),
  4358	                    oracle_right[index].to_bits(),
  4359	                    "right lane {lane} frame {frame}"
  4360	                );
  4361	            }
  4362	        }
  4363	    }
  4364	
  4365	    /// **Restoring one track of a uniform cohort desynchronises the phase, and that falls back.**
  4366	    ///
  4367	    /// Issue #182 S1, the phase leg of [`lanes_uniform`], and the reason the gate is two bit
  4368	    /// compares rather than one. Every lane here is prepared with the same 5 ms lookahead, so the
  4369	    /// shape leg holds for the whole run and never fires. What moves is the *position inside the
  4370	    /// van Herk block*: `commit_lane` writes one lane's `phase` straight out of a payload, and the
  4371	    /// donor below was snapshotted two blocks into its own timeline while the cohort is three
  4372	    /// blocks into its. 256 mod 241 is 15 and 384 mod 241 is 143, so track 0 lands at phase 15
  4373	    /// inside a cohort resting at 143.
  4374	    ///
  4375	    /// Red mutation: drop the phase leg, `state.phase.iter().all(..)`, from `lanes_uniform`. The
  4376	    /// bank then reads `state.phase[0]` — the restored 15 — for all eight lanes, so the seven
  4377	    /// lanes that were *not* restored take their window minimum at the wrong window position and
  4378	    /// run their suffix pass on the wrong block boundary. They diverge from their scalar twins,
  4379	    /// which is the whole-bank failure a per-lane parameter causes when it is assumed uniform.
  4380	    ///
  4381	    /// The scalar arm restores the same payload into track 0 at the same block, so the comparison
  4382	    /// is not "did the restore change anything" — it is "did the restore change anything *for the
  4383	    /// other seven lanes*", which is the only thing the gate is responsible for.
  4384	    #[test]
  4385	    fn a_restore_that_desyncs_the_phase_falls_back() {
  4386	        let values = values_with(-6.0, 100.0, 5.0);
  4387	        let tracks: Vec<[InitialParameterValue; PARAMETER_COUNT * 2]> =
  4388	            (0..8).map(|_| values).collect();
  4389	
  4390	        // The donor: the same program, two blocks into a different signal, so its phase is 15.
  4391	        let mut donor = TruePeakLimiterFactory
  4392	            .prepare(request(&values))
  4393	            .expect("prepare");
  4394	        let mut noise = Noise(0x0D0D_0182);
  4395	        let mut left: Vec<f32> = (0..256).map(|_| noise.next() * 3.0).collect();
  4396	        let mut right: Vec<f32> = (0..256).map(|_| noise.next() * 3.0).collect();
  4397	        render(donor.as_mut(), &mut left, &mut right, 128);
  4398	        let payload = snapshot(donor.as_ref());
  4399	        assert_eq!(
  4400	            read_u32(&payload.1, words::PHASE),
  4401	            256 % 241,
  4402	            "the donor is not at the phase this test is about"
  4403	        );
  4404	
  4405	        let run = cohort_run(&tracks, 8, Some((3, payload)));
  4406	        run.assert_lane_identity("phase-desynchronised cohort");
  4407	    }
  4408	
  4409	    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  4410	    // Issue #182 S2: the earned silence fixed point.
  4411	    //
  4412	    // The family is the compressor's (`compressor/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs`) at a
  4413	    // kernel whose rest state is not all zeros. Two of the three rings rest at exactly `1.0` rather
  4414	    // than `+0.0`, and the argument transfers unchanged because what it needs is that a resting
  4415	    // ring is **uniform**: a read from any cursor position then returns the value a slow path would
  4416	    // have read, so a block that writes only the resting value back leaves it bit-identical
  4417	    // whatever the cursor did.
  4418	    //
  4419	    // This crate is also the one where the fixed point is *exactly* reachable, which the compressor
  4420	    // records as the precondition for engaging at all and does not have: `gain_reduction_db`
  4421	    // approaches `0` dB geometrically, whereas the box terms here live on the `2^-14` grid with
  4422	    // `BOX_GRID * R` below `2^24` at every launch rate, so the running sum arrives at exactly `Wb`,
  4423	    // and the D7 flush terminates the release at exactly `+0.0` rather than near it.
  4424	    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  4425	
  4426	    /// One block of signal, or a block filled with `quiet` — an exact `+0.0` or an exact `-0.0`.
  4427	    ///
  4428	    /// The signal is [`Noise`], the crate's SplitMix64, seeded from the block index so that two
  4429	    /// arms of the same comparison see the same samples and a corpus stays a seed rather than a
  4430	    /// file. It is deliberately *not* a sine: `f32::sin` is a platform transcendental, which
  4431	    /// decision D6 and `clippy.toml`'s `disallowed-methods` (formerly `scripts/check-math-policy.sh`)
  4432	    /// forbid anywhere in `src/` — including in a test module, since the lint scans the file and
  4433	    /// not the `cfg`.
  4434	    fn silence_plane(
  4435	        block: usize,
  4436	        frames: usize,
  4437	        width: usize,
  4438	        quiet: Option<f32>,
  4439	        amplitude: f32,
  4440	        negate: bool,
  4441	    ) -> Vec<f32> {
  4442	        if let Some(fill) = quiet {
  4443	            return vec![fill; frames * width];
  4444	        }
  4445	        let mut noise = Noise(0x5182_0000 ^ (block as u64).wrapping_mul(0x9E37_79B9));
  4446	        (0..frames * width)
  4447	            .map(|_| {
  4448	                let value = noise.next() * amplitude;
  4449	                if negate { -value } else { value }
  4450	            })
  4451	            .collect()
  4452	    }
  4453	
  4454	    /// A core of `L::WIDTH` identically prepared lanes, driven directly through `process_block`.
  4455	    ///
  4456	    /// The same construction `a_nonfinite_block_is_zeroed_reset_and_counted` uses, and for the same
  4457	    /// reason: `process_block` *is* the shipped path — `process` and `process_bank` both end in it
  4458	    /// — and reaching it directly is what lets the control arm suppress the fast path without
  4459	    /// having to change the signal or the parameters to do it.
  4460	    fn silent_core<L: Lane>(ceiling: f32, release: f32, lookahead: f32) -> LimiterCore<L> {
  4461	        let values = values_with(ceiling, release, lookahead);
  4462	        let mut preparation = request(&values);
  4463	        preparation.link_mode = LinkMode::DualMono;
  4464	        let metadata = expected_prepared_metadata(&TRUE_PEAK_LIMITER_DESCRIPTOR, preparation)
  4465	            .expect("metadata");
  4466	        let (left, right) = initial_defaults(&values).expect("defaults");
  4467	        LimiterCore::<L>::new(
  4468	            metadata,
  4469	            vec![left; L::WIDTH].into_boxed_slice(),
  4470	            vec![right; L::WIDTH].into_boxed_slice(),
  4471	        )
  4472	        .expect("core")
  4473	    }
  4474	
  4475	    /// Every word of one core's state, as bits: both cursors, then both channels' whole arenas.
  4476	    ///
  4477	    /// Comparing *this* between the two arms, and not only the rendered samples, is what makes the
  4478	    /// fast path's cursor and phase advances load-bearing. The compressor's version of this test
  4479	    /// records honestly that deleting its cursor advance passes every test in its file, because a
  4480	    /// ring of exact `+0.0` reads the same from every position; reading the state back directly
  4481	    /// closes that gap rather than restating it. `phase` is in the list for the same reason.
  4482	    fn state_bits<L: Lane>(core: &LimiterCore<L>) -> Vec<u32> {
  4483	        let mut words = vec![core.cursors.main, core.cursors.ring];
  4484	        for channel in [&core.left, &core.right] {
  4485	            for plane in [
  4486	                &channel.history,
  4487	                &channel.main_ring,
  4488	                &channel.required_ring,
  4489	                &channel.box_ring,
  4490	                &channel.reduction,
  4491	                &channel.prefix,
  4492	                &channel.box_sum,
  4493	            ] {
  4494	                words.extend(plane.iter().map(|value| value.to_bits()));
  4495	            }
  4496	            words.extend(channel.phase.iter().copied());
  4497	            // The two coefficient ramps, which the fast path must not freeze. A skipped block
  4498	            // advances no ramp, so a claim admitted while a de-zipper window was still open would
  4499	            // strand `current` short of its target for as long as the silence lasted.
  4500	            for ramps in [&channel.limit, &channel.release] {
  4501	                for ramp in ramps.iter() {
  4502	                    words.push(ramp.current.to_bits());
  4503	                    words.push(ramp.target.to_bits());
  4504	                    words.push(ramp.step.to_bits());
  4505	                    words.push(ramp.remaining);
  4506	                }
  4507	            }
  4508	        }
  4509	        words
  4510	    }
  4511	
  4512	    /// What one arm of a silence comparison produced.
  4513	    struct SilenceArm {
  4514	        /// Every rendered sample of every block, both planes.
  4515	        rendered: Vec<u32>,
  4516	        /// The whole instance's state, sampled at the end of every block.
  4517	        states: Vec<u32>,
  4518	        /// Left lane 0's recursive reduction word, at the end of every block.
  4519	        reduction: Vec<u32>,
  4520	        /// Blocks the fast path actually took.
  4521	        engagements: u32,
  4522	    }
  4523	
  4524	    /// Renders `plan` through `core`: `None` is a tone block, `Some(fill)` a constant plane.
  4525	    ///
  4526	    /// `force_slow` withdraws the claim before every block, which is the control arm: it changes
  4527	    /// nothing about the signal, the parameters or the block boundaries, so any difference between
  4528	    /// the arms is the fast path and only the fast path.
  4529	    fn run_silence_arm<L: Lane>(
  4530	        core: &mut LimiterCore<L>,
  4531	        plan: &[Option<f32>],
  4532	        frames: usize,
  4533	        amplitude: f32,
  4534	        force_slow: bool,
  4535	    ) -> SilenceArm {
  4536	        let width = L::WIDTH;
  4537	        let mut arm = SilenceArm {
  4538	            rendered: Vec::new(),
  4539	            states: Vec::new(),
  4540	            reduction: Vec::new(),
  4541	            engagements: 0,
  4542	        };
  4543	        for (block, quiet) in plan.iter().enumerate() {
  4544	            let mut left = silence_plane(block, frames, width, *quiet, amplitude, false);
  4545	            let mut right = silence_plane(block, frames, width, *quiet, amplitude, true);
  4546	            if force_slow {
  4547	                core.silent_fixed_point = false;
  4548	            }
  4549	            core.process_block(&mut left, &mut right, frames);
  4550	            arm.rendered
  4551	                .extend(left.iter().map(|value| value.to_bits()));
  4552	            arm.rendered
  4553	                .extend(right.iter().map(|value| value.to_bits()));
  4554	            arm.states.extend(state_bits(core));
  4555	            arm.reduction.push(core.left.reduction[0].to_bits());
  4556	        }
  4557	        arm.engagements = core.silent_engagements();
  4558	        arm
  4559	    }
  4560	
  4561	    /// Renders `plan` twice at one width, once free and once forced slow, and asserts they agree.
  4562	    fn compare_silence_arms<L: Lane>(
  4563	        label: &str,
  4564	        plan: &[Option<f32>],
  4565	        ceiling: f32,
  4566	        release: f32,
  4567	        amplitude: f32,
  4568	    ) -> SilenceArm {
  4569	        let mut fast = silent_core::<L>(ceiling, release, 5.0);
  4570	        let mut slow = silent_core::<L>(ceiling, release, 5.0);
  4571	        let free = run_silence_arm(&mut fast, plan, 128, amplitude, false);
  4572	        let forced = run_silence_arm(&mut slow, plan, 128, amplitude, true);
  4573	        assert_eq!(
  4574	            forced.engagements, 0,
  4575	            "{label}: the control arm took the fast path, so it is not a control"
  4576	        );
  4577	        assert_eq!(
  4578	            free.rendered, forced.rendered,
  4579	            "{label}: the silent fast path moved a rendered bit"
  4580	        );
  4581	        assert_eq!(
  4582	            free.states, forced.states,
  4583	            "{label}: the silent fast path moved a state word"
  4584	        );
  4585	        free
  4586	    }
  4587	
  4588	    /// A plan of `before` tone blocks, `quiet` silent blocks and `after` tone blocks.
  4589	    fn silence_plan(before: usize, quiet: usize, after: usize) -> Vec<Option<f32>> {
  4590	        let mut plan = vec![None; before];
  4591	        plan.extend(vec![Some(0.0_f32); quiet]);
  4592	        plan.extend(vec![None; after]);
  4593	        plan
  4594	    }
  4595	
  4596	    /// **A settled silent limiter renders exactly the limiter that is never allowed to skip.**
  4597	    ///
  4598	    /// Issue #182 S2, the headline gate, at all three widths. The tone is well under the guarded
  4599	    /// ceiling (`limit = 10^(-7/20) = 0.447` against an amplitude of `0.05`), so `r = 1` at every
  4600	    /// frame and the recursive word never leaves `+0.0`. That is deliberate, and it is the same
  4601	    /// choice the compressor's file explains at length: it isolates the *rings* as the thing that
  4602	    /// has to drain, and it makes the fixed point reachable inside a test-sized run.
  4603	    /// `a_limiter_still_releasing_through_the_silence_is_never_frozen` is the arm that makes the
  4604	    /// recursive word's own leg load-bearing.
  4605	    ///
  4606	    /// What has to drain here is the main delay line, `B = N + 6 = 486` samples at 48 kHz, which is
  4607	    /// 3.8 blocks of 128. The claim is therefore earned at the end of the block in which both the
  4608	    /// line has gone entirely `+0.0` *and* the output has, and the engagement count below is that
  4609	    /// arithmetic read back rather than asserted loosely.
  4610	    ///
  4611	    /// Red mutations: drop `block_is_positive_zero` on either input plane from the admission test;
  4612	    /// drop `is_at_silent_rest` on either channel from the claim; drop `all_exactly_one(&self
  4613	    /// .main_ring)`'s counterpart `block_is_positive_zero(&self.main_ring)`; drop the output test
  4614	    /// from the claim; and — caught by the state comparison rather than the sample comparison —
  4615	    /// delete `self.cursors.advance(..)` or either `advance_rest_phase(..)` from the fast path.
  4616	    #[test]
  4617	    fn a_settled_silent_limiter_renders_exactly_the_never_fast_path() {
  4618	        const SILENT_BLOCKS: usize = 40;
  4619	        let plan = silence_plan(1, SILENT_BLOCKS, 8);
  4620	        let scalar = compare_silence_arms::<f32>("scalar", &plan, -6.0, 100.0, 0.05);
  4621	        let four = compare_silence_arms::<Simd4>("W4", &plan, -6.0, 100.0, 0.05);
  4622	        let eight = compare_silence_arms::<Simd8>("W8", &plan, -6.0, 100.0, 0.05);
