  4737	    /// that restates the value it already holds snaps through `LinearRamp::stationary_at` and
  4738	    /// changes no state at all, so skipping would have been correct. It is kept for two reasons
  4739	    /// that are: the claim must not silently depend on `RAMP_UPDATES` being non-zero, which is a
  4740	    /// tuning constant and not a contract; and it is what makes a restated point a usable
  4741	    /// forced-slow control arm, which is how the compressor's family is built.
