  1240	/// Everything one channel does with one frame, after the peak has been linked.
  1241	///
  1242	/// Frozen operation order; `A` marks a step that is bit-preserving against layout 1 and `B` a step
  1243	/// of the new law.
  1244	///
  1245	/// 1. **required (A)** `r = select(P > limit, limit / P, 1)`. `P > limit >= 10^(-25/20)` implies
  1246	///    `P > 0`, so the divide is always defined; it is a divide and not a reciprocal because the
  1247	///    unlimited case must be exactly `1.0`.
  1248	/// 2. **write (A)** `r` is stored at the write cursor, before the minimum filter reads the window.
  1249	/// 3. **minimum (B)** the van Herk window minimum of each lane.
  1250	/// 4. **quantise (B)** `m_q = floor(m * 2^14) * 2^-14`; both scalings are exact.
  1251	/// 5. **box (B)** `S += m_q - m_q[n-Wb]`, read before write so `Wb == R` reads the slot it is about
  1252	///    to overwrite; `s = S / Wb`.
  1253	/// 6. **release (B)** `d = max(1 - s, fma(c, (1 - s) - d, d))`, then the D7 flush. This is the only
  1254	///    `fma` and the only recursive word in the crate. Working in the reduction domain is what makes
  1255	///    the decay terminate at exactly `+0.0`, and therefore `g` at exactly `1.0`.
  1256	/// 7. **output (A)** read-before-write on the main ring gives a delay of exactly `B = N + 6`;
  1257	///    `y = select(bypass, z, z * g)` keeps the bypass path bit-exact including signed zero.
  1258	/// # The uniform-cohort form
  1259	///
  1260	/// [`channel_frame_uniform`] is the same seven steps for a cohort [`lanes_uniform`] has accepted
  1261	/// (#182 S1): steps 3 and 5 run lane-wide there instead of lane by lane. It is a separate function
  1262	/// rather than a const parameter on this one so that neither form carries the other's branch —
  1263	/// and, since round 2, so that the uniform form can be handed pre-split ring views and pre-resolved
  1264	/// slot indices that this one, addressing the arena lane by lane, cannot use. The whole-bank
  1265	/// decision is taken once, in [`limiter_block`].

